          ],
          "text": "ABSTRACT",
          "reading_order": 1,
          "tags": [
            "paper_abstract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "para",
          "bbox": [
            95,
            121,
            525,
            300
          ],
          "text": "In recent years, the increasing shortage of raw material, in particular, the\nproblems of environmental pollution and energy consumption facing the domestic\npulping and papermaking industry, makes people attach great importance to\nre-utility of recycled fibers, namely waste paper. The rapid increase in utility rate\nof waste paper is an important tendency in the international papermaking industry.\nSecondary fibers as an important fiber source can not only alleviate the paradox\nbetween the lack of papermaking raw materials and energy consumption, but also\nplay essential role in keeping up the ecological balance by decreasing the\nenvironmental pollution problems.",
          "reading_order": 2,
          "tags": [
            "paper_abstract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "para",
          "bbox": [
            96,
            303,
            525,
            361
          ],
          "text": "Damage mechanism of paper, a newly developed science, combines the damage\ntheory with the paper structure. In this paper, damage theory is further introduced to\nstudy the degradation of fiber and paper property.",
          "reading_order": 3,
          "tags": [
            "paper_abstract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "para",
          "bbox": [
            96,
            364,
            525,
            421
          ],
          "text": "Firstly, the changes in property of recycled fibers and paper were studied.\n\n\nFiber properties such as fiber length, strength, DP and crystallization and those of\n\n\npaper such as tensile, tearing strength, and RBA are analyzed",
          "reading_order": 4,
          "tags": [
            "paper_abstract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "para",
          "bbox": [
            96,
            424,
            525,
            522
          ],
          "text": "The series of changes ultimately were caused by hornification of recycled fibers.\nTherefore, the hornification problems of recycled fibers including the affecting\nfactors, occurring rules , that sort of things were then studied. In the meaning time,\nthe ways of resolution of hornification were discussed, from which some\nmechanisms and reasons of it were observed.",
          "reading_order": 5,
          "tags": [
            "paper_abstract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "para",
          "bbox": [
            96,
            526,
            526,
            605
          ],
          "text": "In the end, damage theory was introduced. The damage factors suitable for\nrecycled fiber damage were defined elementally, with which involvement rules of\npaper strength with damage variables were studied. Here, the environmental\ndamage—aging due to heat was simply involved.",
          "reading_order": 6,
          "tags": [
            "paper_abstract"
          ]
        },
